        {
          "question": "e-13178",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $|k-1| \\leq 4.$ So, we first need to solve for $k{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|k-1|\\le 4 \\\\ -4\\le k-1\\le 4 \\\\ -3\\le k\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the above inequality are $-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5.$ \n\nTherefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA = \\{0,\\pm1,\\pm2,\\pm3,4,5 \\}.\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
