      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-13179",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi x}{2} & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in\\mathbb Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx = 0,\\, \\pm 2 ,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA= \\{0,\\, \\pm 2 ,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\\}.\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038440/example-13179.json",
          "file_sha256": "28e60783d566095214eeb0df16b09bf10b0897d93581b25abd8291115857dc79"
